diff --git a/advisories/CVE-2026-53260/analysis.md b/advisories/CVE-2026-53260/analysis.md
index 5f3e7a7..b12ae4b 100644
--- a/advisories/CVE-2026-53260/analysis.md
+++ b/advisories/CVE-2026-53260/analysis.md
@@ -105,3 +105,49 @@ old config/LSM/program/device/CPU policy. The encrypted-key module is actually
 loaded on one reporting node, demonstrating why absence from a default preload
 list cannot establish fleet-wide non-exposure. Intel/AMD KVM vendor module
 observations do not by themselves prove nested VMX or IntelPT capabilities.
+
+## Follow-up: storage workload and necessary RT condition
+
+The operator clarified that storage runs no user workloads. This removes a
+tenant process route but does not establish that host backup/NFS TCP listeners
+never reach `reqsk_queue_hash_req`, or that listener closure cannot race its
+request timer on an affected RT build. The primary fix explicitly identifies
+PREEMPT_RT preemption between timer arming and reference initialization, followed
+by listener closure and timer expiry. Remote requests alone are not proof of
+attacker control over that full sequence, and absence of VPSes is not proof of
+its host-path exclusion.
+
+The frozen storage record contains no usable booted/reported release, exact
+configuration, or complete retained history. In particular it cannot bind storage
+to the independently archived non-RT .95 build. Resolution needs positive
+`CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT=n` evidence for the actual applicable storage builds and
+period, a supported pre-introduction/fixed kernel history, or a source-backed
+exclusion of the necessary host listener lifecycle throughout that period. A
+current-only non-RT statement without build/time scope cannot establish earlier
+safety or a mitigation date. The role set remains `node` and `storage`; the
+normal evaluation therefore retains the missing-evidence storage result as
+unknown. No history override, build acceptance or manual status is added.
+
+### Operator observation of the running storage kernel
+
+In this follow-up the operator supplied this direct observation from
+`backuper2.prg.vpsfree.cz`:
+
+```text
+[root@backuper2.prg.vpsfree.cz] zgrep -i preempt_rt /proc/config.gz
+# CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT is not set
+```
+
+This positive runtime configuration evidence excludes the necessary RT lock
+implementation on that running storage kernel, independently of whether storage
+has user processes. It is an operator observation after the frozen collection;
+no exact kernel/configuration digest, boot identity, historical start time or
+January-to-snapshot scope accompanies it. It therefore establishes the current
+necessary-gate exclusion without proving the older retained interval safe or
+supplying a mitigation timestamp. The frozen snapshot and consumed submission
+baselines remain unchanged. The reviewed Node161-only English/Czech note now
+conveys that current necessary-gate exclusion while explicitly retaining the
+unknown earlier configuration. The all-period state remains unknown because the
+period question is unanswered and the frozen history has no supporting storage
+build evidence. No evidence JSON, attestation or per-node evaluation is edited
+by hand; the normal evaluator propagates the dossier-authored note.
